.claude
.git
# This package declares "mirador" (and react-i18next, i18next, react, react-dom) as
# peerDependencies (the host app must supply a single shared instance) but also installs its own
# copies as devDependencies (for its own standalone demo). Since it's consumed elsewhere via a raw
# file: link to this checkout (not a published, pruned package), those dev-only copies would
# otherwise shadow the host's when this package's own code resolves them -- splitting
# module-level singletons (e.g. Mirador's OSDReferences) and, for react-i18next, React Context
# identity (useTranslation() then can't find the real I18nextProvider) across separate instances.
node_modules/mirador
node_modules/react-i18next
node_modules/i18next
